<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy — App Privacy Manifest

  Required by Apple since May 2024. Missing or incorrect manifests cause
  TestFlight processing rejections.

  What this manifest declares:
  1. NSPrivacyTracking = false: The app does NOT track users.
  2. NSPrivacyTrackingDomains = []: No tracking domains.
  3. NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes = []: No data collection for tracking or linking.
  4. NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes = []: No required-reason APIs are used.

  Required-reason API analysis (WWDC23-10060):
    - File timestamp APIs: NOT USED. The app does not read file modification times.
    - System boot time APIs: NOT USED. No CACurrentMediaTime/mach_absolute_time.
    - Disk space APIs: NOT USED. No NSFileManager disk space queries.
    - Active keyboards API: NOT USED. No UITextInputMode queries.
    - User defaults APIs: NOT USED. Credentials are stored in Keychain (Security
      framework), not UserDefaults. See KeychainService.swift.

  Data collection analysis:
    - The app connects to user-specified Pulse servers on their own infrastructure.
    - Credentials (server URL, bearer token) are stored locally in the iOS Keychain.
    - No data is sent to the developer (Beyond Kaira) or any third party.
    - Analytics data flows from Pulse servers to the app, not the reverse.

  This is a "zero collection" app: all data stays on the user's device and their
  own Pulse server. The manifest reflects this honestly.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!-- The app does not engage in tracking as defined by Apple. -->
    <key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
    <false/>

    <!-- No tracking domains are contacted. -->
    <key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
    <array/>

    <!-- No data is collected for tracking or linking to the user. -->
    <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
    <array/>

    <!--
      Required-reason APIs used by the app.
      Empty because none of the privacy-sensitive APIs are used:
        - NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp: NOT USED
        - NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategorySystemBootTime: NOT USED
        - NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryDiskSpace: NOT USED
        - NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryActiveKeyboards: NOT USED
        - NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults: NOT USED (Keychain only)
    -->
    <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
    <array/>
</dict>
</plist>
